 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm certain capital improvement projects of the New Rochelle city school district",
    "basePrintNo": "S8044",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8044-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "New Rochelle, City of",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S8044\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act to legalize, validate, ratify and confirm certain capital\nimprovement projects of the New Rochelle city school district\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo allow for an extension for filing state aid for capital improvement\nprojects for the New Rochelle City School District.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 is the legislative intent which finds that the capital\nimprovement projects, which were approved by the school district and\neligible for certain state aid, were designated project numbers\n0001-007, 0002-006,0004-004,0012-006,0006-004, 0003-006, 0001-009,\n0001-010, 7999-001, 7999-002 by the State Education Department. A\nrequired filing for eligibility for aid was not made by the district in\na timely manner.\n\nSection 2 validates all preliminary work done by the school district to\nobtain the Commissioner of Education's approval of aforementioned\nprojects.\n\nSection 3 directs the Education Department to consider the approved\ncosts of the aforementioned projects as valid and proper obligations of\nthe New Rochelle City School District.\n\nSection 4 is the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nDuring a recent review of the status of the New Rochelle City School\nDistrict's capital construction projects, projects were found to have\npassed the deadline for submission of the Final Building Project Report\nto the State Education Department (SED). A copy of the Certificate of\nCompletion for this project either did not reach the appropriate indi-\nvidual or was somehow misplaced. As a result, the report was not\nprepared and submitted prior to the required SED deadline.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
